# Docker build context for packages/server/Dockerfile (context = repo root).
# The image needs only the root manifests, packages/shared and packages/server;
# everything else just makes the upload to the build host slower, and a local
# node_modules would be copied over the one npm installs inside the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
.github
.expo
**/.expo
**/dist
mobile
docs
tasks
scripts
*.bundle
*.patch
*.log
# Generated/served at runtime, never baked into the image (see DEPLOYMENT.md §12).
packages/server/mushaf-pages
packages/server/uploads
packages/server/reports
packages/server/certificates
packages/server/.env
packages/server/.env.*
# Local secrets never enter the build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Local tool state.
graphify-out
ruvector.db
.agents
analysis
agents
# The image needs mobile's manifest (npm workspace resolution) but nothing else.
!mobile/package.json
